Verifies [expr.unary.noexcept]/3: the noexcept operator correctly
returns true for non-throwing expressions (builtins, literals, noexcept
functions, destructors) and false for throw-expressions and non-noexcept
function calls.  Historic entry in STANDARD_COVERAGE.md claimed the
operator "always evaluates to false" but the implementation actually
follows the standard.
